Adds a per-function register PIC site namespace (A1)

The register backend's named-property instructions carried the shared stack
inline-cache slot index. A1 gives them their own dense per-function numbering,
a JSFunctionBytecode field to hold the count, a per-frame base pointer carried
on every execution and resume path, and serialization of the count.

  * quickjs.c: JSRegPIC forward declaration; JSFunctionBytecode.regvm_pic and
    .regvm_pic_count; JSRegRun.pic set at record fill, entry and threaded
    rebind; dense site assignment derived from the ROP format string; site
    operands validated against regvm_pic_count; regvm_pic_count written and
    read in the register program header; ROP_get_length gains a site operand;
    the stack-IC helpers are bypassed for register code until A3/A4 install
    fills and hits.
  * quickjs-regvm.h: REGVM_FORMAT_VERSION 11 -> 12.

The site position is taken from regvm_rop_fmt rather than hard-coded, because
it differs between the generic and fused spellings of one operation:
get_field is "rras" (site at index 3) while get_local_field_0 is "ras" (site
at index 2). A fixed index wrote the dense number over the atom for every
"rras"/"ruas" opcode and left the real site stale.

Shape ownership, cache fill and hit paths are A2-A4 and are not in this patch.
